<Layout title="Virginia Tech doctor in Blacksburg | Kin & Campus" description="A board-certified pediatrician in Blacksburg for Virginia Tech students. Ongoing care, refills, sick visits, and forms — coordinated with the hometown doctor.">
<div class="w hero2"><div><div class="eyebrow">Pediatric care for Virginia Tech students</div><h1>A pediatrician in Blacksburg for Virginia Tech students.</h1><p class="lead">A board-certified physician right here in town — looking after them the years they are away from you on campus. Asthma, ADHD, anxiety medications, refills, sick visits, and university forms. Their hometown doctor stays in the loop.</p><p class="hero-cta"><a class="btn" href={href("join")}>Reserve a spot</a><a class="lnk" href={href("parents")}>For parents &rarr;</a><a class="lnk" href={href("students")}>For students &rarr;</a></p></div>
<img class="art" src={href("photos/drillfield-fall.jpg")} width="678" height="452" alt="Fall leaves on the Drillfield, Burruss Hall across the green">
</div>
<div class="w"><div class="trust"><div><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-heart"/></svg><b>The plan stays active</b><span>Ongoing prescriptions and chronic care continue in town, including over holidays and finals.</span></div><div><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-clock"/></svg><b>A doctor eight minutes from campus</b><span>Usually same week, and often same day. The panel stays small so visits stay available.</span></div><div><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-shield"/></svg><b>You stay in the loop</b><span>With the student's consent, we keep you and their hometown doctor informed.</span></div></div></div>
<section><div class="w split"><div><div class="eyebrow">For parents</div><h2>They're far from home. We are local.</h2><p>A board-certified pediatrician nearby. Check-ins around midterms and holidays, and the doctor who has known them since kindergarten stays informed.</p><p><a class="lnk" href={href("parents")}>How we look after them &rarr;</a></p></div>
<svg class="art" viewBox="0 0 600 190" role="img" aria-label="You, Kin and Campus, and your student, connected"><path d="M112 80Q190 10 265 66M335 66Q410 10 488 80" fill="none" stroke="#C9A24B" stroke-width="4" stroke-dasharray="2 10" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="70" cy="82" r="42" fill="#6B2737"/><circle cx="70" cy="70" r="12" fill="#F6EFE4"/><path d="M46 104q24-26 48 0z" fill="#F6EFE4"/><circle cx="530" cy="82" r="42" fill="#C9A24B"/><circle cx="530" cy="70" r="12" fill="#2A1A1E"/><path d="M506 104q24-26 48 0z" fill="#2A1A1E"/><circle cx="300" cy="78" r="40" fill="#9CAF98"/><path d="M272 84L300 58 328 84v22H272z" fill="#FBF7F0" stroke="#6B2737" stroke-width="3"/><rect x="293" y="90" width="14" height="16" fill="#C9A24B"/><g font-family="DM Sans,sans-serif" font-size="15" font-weight="700" fill="currentColor" text-anchor="middle"><text x="70" y="150">You</text><text x="300" y="150">Kin &amp; Campus</text><text x="530" y="150">Your student</text></g></svg></div></section>
<section style="padding-top:0"><div class="w"><div class="eyebrow">What a parent wants, in town</div><h2>Four things we hold while they're here.</h2><div class="grid"><div class="card"><div class="num">1</div><h3>Seamless chronic care</h3><p>Their established care plan stays active. We manage ongoing prescriptions, navigate holidays and finals, and update you when things shift.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="num">2</div><h3>A trained eye in town</h3><p>A local pediatrician living right here in Blacksburg — watching out for them the way you would if you were just eight minutes away.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="num">3</div><h3>Building adult health habits</h3><p>College is where healthcare transitions from parents managing the details to young adults owning it. We help them learn how to navigate appointments and care on their own.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="num">4</div><h3>Aligned care</h3><p>Student, physician, and parents working together. We talk things through in the room, keeping you and their hometown doctor connected.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section><div class="w"><div class="eyebrow">Once you join</div><h2>A parent starts. The student keeps the number.</h2><div class="grid"><div class="card"><h3>You reach out</h3><p>Tell us who is heading to Blacksburg, and we'll set up an introductory call. No intake forms hidden behind generic portals.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>They meet their doctor</h3><p>An initial visit in town to establish care before classes kick into gear.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>The number is theirs</h3><p>Direct text access from then on. Sick visits when they need them, plus check-ins around high-stress windows.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="band"><div class="w"><div class="eyebrow">Privacy</div><h2>Privacy respected. Parents kept in the loop.</h2><p>Once your student turns 18, their medical chart legally belongs to them. Before care begins, we establish a clear communication agreement together so you aren't left in the dark—while respecting their privacy as an adult. Plus, their hometown doctor receives a clinical update the very same day. <a class="lnk2" href={href("privacy")}>How sharing works &rarr;</a></p></div></section>
<section><div class="w"><h2>Built for them. Backed for you.</h2><div class="grid"><div class="card"><h3>For your student</h3><p>A local doctor in Blacksburg who treats them like an adult, respects their privacy, and is a text away when something comes up.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>For you</h3><p>A board-certified pediatrician looking after their health, keeping their hometown care plan intact, and looping you in when it matters.</p></div></div>
<p class="cite" style="max-width:640px;margin-top:28px">An ER visit can cost hundreds of dollars — or several thousand on a high-deductible plan. If it is a true emergency, call 911. Large-employer plans averaged $646 out of pocket. <a href="https://www.kff.org/health-costs/emergency-department-visits-exceed-affordability-threshold-for-many-consumers-with-private-insurance/">KFF / Peterson-Kaiser Health System Tracker</a>, 2019 claims (published 2022).</p>
<p style="margin-top:28px"><a class="btn" href={href("join")}>Reserve a spot</a></p></div></section>
</Layout>
